WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.350
Another Thing Dr. Bright is not allowed to
do at the Foundation: No, Dr. Bright, you

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.760
can't have a pet SCP!

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.510
We don't care how many O5 Council members
agree to it, or if there have been precedents

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.140
set by previous cases.

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:19.320
Dr. Bright has not proven himself responsible
enough to have a pet SCP of any kind.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.590
We gave him a goldfish, and he promised to
keep it alive for a year.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.590
He failed.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.980
We gave him a potted plant, and he promised
to take care of that.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.470
It lasted a week.

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.600
Giving Dr. Bright a dangerous anomaly to care
for would be a huge security risk, and giving

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.899
him a harmless SCP would certainly constitute
animal cruelty.

00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:40.969
And no, he absolutely cannot have SCP-999.

